Z||000003||Mach10||11-15-2001||05:47 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>General "uneducated" consensus seems to think that Saddam is next. (Nobody but the military <I>really</I> knows, of course.)<BR>But what about all those "baby bin Ladens" being churned out by the so-called "religious" schools in Pakistan? <BR>They are as rabid as bin Laden, and (I would suspect) fairly numerous. <BR>Should we be looking at a campaign against Pakistan (or some of it's organizations)?<BR>I think they may turn around and bite us when it becomes politically expedient.<BR>Anybody else? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Going to war with Pakistan would be VERY dangerous. Brand new Nuclear power. India would jump in, and both of them would vaporize each other. <BR>Pakistan has some militants, but so far, their government is still in control. It's going to be a sticky mess, no matter which way you go about it...<P>BTW: I'm FULLY aware that the US Nuclear capabilities far exceed pakistans, but the use of nuclear force would propagate into a global incident. The US would not strike first. After a short ground/air skirmish, Pakistan would let fly some missiles. Then India. Then china, Then russia, Then USA etc... A better idea would be to work WITH The pakistani government to liquify the militant groups as thouroughly as possible.<P><BR>EDIT: Also, remember that Pakistan has been cooperating fully so far... What reason is there to expect any less in the future?<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||13
