Z||000005||Raydar||11-15-2001||06:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>  ...Also, remember that Pakistan has been cooperating fully so far... What reason is there to expect any less in the future?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No concrete reason, really. Unless the militants gain control of the government. Happened in Afghanistan. (Of course, it seems like Afghanistan has changed governments like most people change underwear.) Happened in Iran in the 70s. <BR>I did say that maybe we should target the militant groups. If they gain control of Pakistan's nukes, it could make us have a very bad day. <BR>I don't think we should target Pakistan's present government, unless they double-cross us. Not that there's any evidence that that is going to happen.   <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||11-15-2001||07:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B> No concrete reason, really. Unless the militants gain control of the government. Happened in Afghanistan. (Of course, it seems like Afghanistan has changed governments like most people change underwear.) Happened in Iran in the 70s. <BR>I did say that maybe we should target the militant groups. If they gain control of Pakistan's nukes, it could make us have a very bad day. <BR>I don't think we should target Pakistan's present government, unless they double-cross us. Not that there's any evidence that that is going to happen.   <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>'Zactly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And yeah, I acknowledge the point about Osama. Let this be a lesson to you. KEEP THE CIA FROM TRAINING THE PAKISTANI GOVERNMENT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
